===Etymology===
{{compound|en|air|time}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-airtime.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[duration]] during which a [[radio]] or [[television]] [[program]] (or part of one) is [[transmitted]].
#: {{ux|en|Can you get me some '''airtime''' for my latest single?}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The [[duration]] spent [[talk]]ing during a conversation.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.smartbrief.com/original/2017/05/critical-your-teams-culture-equal-air-time|title=Critical to your team's culture: Equal air time|date=2017-05-17|accessdate=2021-09-15|work=SmartBrief|passage= Let them know you’re looking to create a loosely held balance of '''air time''' and want to hear from everyone.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023| title=Birnam Wood|author=Eleanor Catton| page=109| passage=And all sorts of people who have traditionally been excluded are now being let in and given a voice, and they're pushing ''you'' out and reducing ''your'' '''airtime''', and threatening ''your'' privilege, {{...}}}}
# The [[chargeable]] use of a [[mobile phone]], either in minutes or in units dependent on the use or traffic.
# The period during which a person riding a [[rollercoaster]] or similar ride experiences a feeling of [[weightlessness]].

